If you want to send the selected group back, just use a little JSON like this so I can read it reliably:

{
  "solution": [<selected_item>, <selected_item>, ...]
}

This just shows the shape I expect: the "solution" entry is an array where each placeholder like <selected_item> stands in for one chosen student's identifier. It's only a sketch of the format, not the actual selection — you'll replace each placeholder with the real identifiers from the instance.

Please make sure you use the exact identifiers given in the instance input — do not rename them or invent new labels.
- for example: "Valid identifiers look like plain numbers such as “1” or “23”, single capital letters like “A” or “B”, or a capital letter followed by digits like “A1” or “X7”."

Many teams face this: the marketing lead must nominate exactly the requested number of campaign concepts, and it’s better to present a spread of approaches rather than six clones of the same idea. The way to check is simple — for a given selection, add up the dissimilarity between every pair of chosen items; the selection with the largest total difference is preferred. No item can be picked twice and the number is fixed. The detailed list is below.

